{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1053682-gotv-2e-your-masques","id":1053682,"title":"[GotV 2E] Your Masques","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-23T00:35:24-08:00","id":1053682,"title":"[GotV 2E] Your Masques","content":"Topic for sharing and making your own Masques \u2018trees\u2019 for particular Guardians characters. For inspirations, we have 49 classic Masques in <b>Guardians of Veil</b> Order book.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Notice:</i></b> I put Skill Specialties and Merits lists as <i>propositions</i> \u2013 each character choose his own particular complete for each Masque.<br /> <br /> For ease of reference \u2013 particular dots effects of Masque Merit from 2E <b>Mage</b> corebook:<br /> <br /> <b>Identity (\u2022): </b>Choose a Virtue and Vice different than that of your character. While in the Masque, your character benefits from those traits instead of her own.<br /> <b>Competency (\u2022\u2022): </b>Choose Skill Specialties equal to the Masque Merit dots. Your character uses those Specialties instead of her own while in the Masque.<br /> <b>Diffusion (\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Choose a new Signature Nimbus (see p. 89). While in the Masque, your character uses that Nimbus instead of her own.<br /> <b>The Code (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Choose two Acts of Hubris your character would normally suffer. While in the Masque, your character does not risk Wisdom for those acts.<br /> <b>Immersion (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Choose up to five Merit dots. When your character dons her Masque, she gains access to these Merits. These Merits must be logical parts of the identity, at Storyteller discretion, and cannot include further Masques.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Good Death ( Prudence \\ Envy from GotV book )</span></b><br /> <br /> The Good Death is an assassin. He dispatches his targets as efficiently as possible and pretends to have a detached attitude toward his victims. Mercy is not an option, unless it tempts the one weakness in his character. The Good Death doesn\u2019t really kill for money or for a cause. He kills to pretend he has power over death. In a moment of honesty, a religious Good Death might say he envies God. With every kill, he reaffirms that he, and not some higher power, is the master of his fate.<br /> <br /> <b>Identity (\u2022): </b>Prudent \\ Violent ( thought about \u2018Efficient\u2019 as Vice, but it would simply double Prudent Virtue in gameplay )<br /> <b>Competency (\u2022\u2022): </b>Skill Specialties \u2013 Stealth ( Shadowing ), Weaponry or Firearms ( Any chosen )<br /> <b>Diffusion (\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Signature Nimbus \u2013 Long shadows and cold is entrenching items.<br /> <b>The Code (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Acts of Hubris \u2013 Planned murder, Impassionate killing ( if plans derail )<br /> <b>Immersion (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Merits \u2013 Professional Training ( Assassin \u2013 Asset Skills: Stealth and Weaponry or Firearms ), Fast Reflexes, Meditative Mind, Trained Observer, Allies ( Assassins )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-23-2017, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T05:39:26-08:00","id":1053769,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Golden Hand ( Prudence \\ Greed </b><b>from GotV book )</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> This Masques is used in tactics based on social, economic or even magical bounding and extortion of target. Golden Hands balance their materialism and common sense to survive. Based on the merchants of ancient cultures, the Masque has become that of the average urban worker. Golden Hands are shopkeepers, sales people and service employees: people whom the supernatural world either ignores or treats as victims. The order doesn\u2019t believe that every normal person is a Golden Hand, but that the Masque is emblematic of the modern age. It\u2019s true that the average Golden Hand is materialistic (and cowardly, because a Golden Hand views her life as her most prized property), but desperation can inspire her. Under stress, average people can devise cunning plans capable of snaring those too blinded by supernatural power to notice the threats.<br /> <br /> <b>Identity (\u2022): </b>Prudent \\ Greedy<br /> <b>Competency (\u2022\u2022): </b>Skill Specialties \u2013 Persuasion ( Deals ), Empathy ( Motivations ), Socialize ( Clients )<br /> <b>Diffusion (\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Signature Nimbus \u2013 For Mage Sight, literally everything that Golden Hand touches becomes gold! Or rather have golden radiance.<br /> <b>The Code (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Acts of Hubris \u2013 Forcing a sapient being (whether a Sleeper, spirit, or anything else) to act counter to its interests, Binding being to a task based on previous contract<br /> <b>Immersion (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Merits \u2013 Professional Training (Professional), Good Time Management, Indomitable, Multilingual, Patient, Closed Book, Contacts, Fast-Talking, Fixer, Iron Will, Table Turner","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-23-2017, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T06:37:46-07:00","id":1517641,"title":"","content":"All of the The The Exactors (Prudence) Masques:<br /> Golden Hand (Prudence/Greed\u200b)<br /> Good Death (Prudence/Envy\u200b)<br /> Binder of Night (Prudence/Gluttony)<br /> Eye of Mars (Prudence/Wrath)<br /> Lord Chain (Prudence/Lust)<br /> Scepter (Prudence/Pride)<br /> Shieldbearer (Prudence/Sloth)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27472,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","user":"Phoenix853457","date":". 08-11-2023, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T08:15:44-07:00","id":1517649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1053682-gotv-2e-your-masques#post1053682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Topic for sharing and making your own Masques \u2018trees\u2019 for particular Guardians characters. For inspirations, we have 49 classic Masques in <b>Guardians of Veil</b> Order book.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Notice:</i></b> I put Skill Specialties and Merits lists as <i>propositions</i> \u2013 each character choose his own particular complete for each Masque.<br /> <br /> For ease of reference \u2013 particular dots effects of Masque Merit from 2E <b>Mage</b> corebook:<br /> <br /> <b>Identity (\u2022): </b>Choose a Virtue and Vice different than that of your character. While in the Masque, your character benefits from those traits instead of her own.<br /> <b><b>Competency (\u2022\u2022): </b>Choose Skill Specialties equal to the Masque Merit dots. Your character uses those Specialties instead of her own while in the Masque.</b><br /> <b>Diffusion (\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Choose a new Signature Nimbus (see p. 89). While in the Masque, your character uses that Nimbus instead of her own.<br /> <b>The Code (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Choose two Acts of Hubris your character would normally suffer. While in the Masque, your character does not risk Wisdom for those acts.<br /> <b>Immersion (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Choose up to five Merit dots. When your character dons her Masque, she gains access to these Merits. These Merits must be logical parts of the identity, at Storyteller discretion, and cannot include further Masques.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I just got a doubt regarding COMPETENCY, do you get more specialties as the masque value grows (and that is why it says &quot;equal to the Masque Merit dots&quot;) or just 2, since you have 2 dots when you get this ability. It would be clearer if it said 2, otherwise it is a bit more convoluted when you have Masque 5, and then spend 2 merit dots for a new Masque.<br /> <br /> Just a nitpick from my side, but it is very confusing for a non native english speaker.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T09:59:53-07:00","id":1517652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1053682-gotv-2e-your-masques?p=1517649#post1517649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just got a doubt regarding COMPETENCY, do you get more specialties as the masque value grows (and that is why it says &quot;equal to the Masque Merit dots&quot;) or just 2, since you have 2 dots when you get this ability. It would be clearer if it said 2, otherwise it is a bit more convoluted when you have Masque 5, and then spend 2 merit dots for a new Masque.<br /> <br /> Just a nitpick from my side, but it is very confusing for a non native english speaker.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Whenever it says Merit dots, you count the total amount of dots in that Merit, not just the dots you had when you first bought that Merit.<br /> <br /> Additional Masques counts as they're at the same level as the original Masque Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T12:32:33-07:00","id":1517653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1053682-gotv-2e-your-masques?p=1517652#post1517652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whenever it says Merit dots, you count the total amount of dots in that Merit, not just the dots you had when you first bought that Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>And every level after the 2nd, you get a new specialty??<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1053682-gotv-2e-your-masques?p=1517652#post1517652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additional Masques counts as they're at the same level as the original Masque Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you buy a new Masque (for 2 Merit dots), you get 5 merit dots (Immersion), plus 5 specialties? That is 10 Experiences worth, and not counting the other benefits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So that means that Masque is the most cost effective merit ever! Am I calculating that right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T13:55:25-07:00","id":1517656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1053682-gotv-2e-your-masques?p=1517653#post1517653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And every level after the 2nd, you get a new specialty??</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1053682-gotv-2e-your-masques?p=1517653#post1517653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you buy a new Masque (for 2 Merit dots), you get 5 merit dots (Immersion), plus 5 specialties? That is 10 Experiences worth, and not counting the other benefits.<br /> <br /> So that means that Masque is the most cost effective merit ever! Am I calculating that right?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of which is mutually exclusive. If you have Masque at 5 dots, and two additional Masques, you'll have 15 Specialties and 15 Merit dots you can't use without using a Masque, and even when using a Masque you're still unable to access 10 Merit dots and at least 13 Specialties (10 from the other two Masques, 3 from starting Specalties, and any number bought with XP or through Professional Training).<br /> You also lose access to any Interdisciplinary Specialty and Area of Expertise Merits you might have on the character (unless your Masque shares Specialties, which means you gained literally nothing, if your ST even allows that since the point of a Masque is to be different from your regular self).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T08:25:51-07:00","id":1519633,"title":"","content":"All of the The Beloved (Charity) Masques:<br /> Average Son (Charity/Wrath)<br /> Holy Concubine (Charity/Lust)<br /> Lancet Master (Charity/Greed)<br /> Lord Incarnadine (Charity/Pride)<br /> Prince of Feasts (Charity/Gluttony)<br /> Silver Cestus (Charity/Envy)<br /> Weaver of Whispers (Charity/Sloth)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27472,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","user":"Phoenix853457","date":". 08-07-2023, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T20:13:45-07:00","id":1519922,"title":"","content":"Apart from the ones in the Order book, what about ones specifically tailored for a certain type of 